{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi. I’ve been having trouble swallowing again—like food gets stuck in my throat. It hurts, especially when I try to eat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And does it happen more with solids or liquids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Mostly solids. I haven’t eaten anything today because it just hurts too much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You mentioned pain—does it hurt only when you swallow, or is there a constant soreness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s there all the time, but worse when I swallow. I feel like I’m choking, and I’m scared I might aspirate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds really distressing. I know you’ve had this before—last time, they thought it was due to residue in your throat and gave you some swallowing techniques."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, they said to cover my trach when I swallow. But I also remember being told to tuck my chin. It’s hard to do both at once."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll get the speech team to help you with that again. For now, we’ll keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—until we figure things out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s fine. I’m just worried this is something new."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve checked your labs and chest X-ray. Everything looks stable—no infection, no lung issues. Your trach site looks clean too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not my trach causing this?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The interventional pulmonology team saw you and said your trach is fine. They don’t think it’s the cause."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2169-10-15 19:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good to know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2169-10-16 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. The ENT team did a bedside scope yesterday. They saw some nasal swelling and a deviated septum, but nothing that explains your swallowing issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2169-10-16 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s causing the pain and the feeling of food getting stuck?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2169-10-16 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re still working on that. You’re scheduled for a video swallow test today—that’ll show us how your throat and esophagus are moving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2169-10-16 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2169-10-16 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s not painful. You’ll swallow some barium-coated foods while they take X-ray videos. It helps us see if food is going where it should."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2169-10-16 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, just got the results from your video swallow. Good news—no aspiration. You’re not breathing food into your lungs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2169-10-16 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. But why do I keep coughing after I swallow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2169-10-16 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The speech team noticed that too. But on the video, there was no food in your airway. They think it’s due to throat sensitivity—your nerves are a bit overreacting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2169-10-16 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. So I’m safe to eat?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2169-10-16 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they think you can start a regular diet. But we’ll make sure you use the swallowing techniques—like covering your trach—to help things move smoothly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2169-10-16 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. But can we go over the steps again? I keep forgetting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2169-10-16 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. For solids: take one bite, then swallow three times. For liquids: two swallows per sip. And cover your trach with your finger each time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2169-10-16 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And what about the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2169-10-16 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve given you Tylenol and ibuprofen. They should help. We’re also checking your blood sugar because it was high this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2169-10-16 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "High sugar? I don’t have diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2169-10-16 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily, but your fasting sugars have been in the 160s–170s. We checked your A1c, and it’s 7.9, which suggests prediabetes or early diabetes. We’ll talk more about that before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2169-10-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got the barium swallow results. It shows moderate esophageal dysmotility—your esophagus isn’t squeezing food down as well as it should."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2169-10-17 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why food feels stuck?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2169-10-17 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be contributing. We didn’t see this before, so it might be new. We recommend seeing a gastroenterologist after discharge to look into it further."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2169-10-17 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Is it serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2169-10-17 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s manageable. It may explain your symptoms, and there are treatments. But for now, you’re doing well—you’ve been eating without trouble, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2169-10-17 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, actually. The pain is much better, and I haven’t choked once since I started using the technique."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2169-10-17 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’ll keep you on ibuprofen for pain and make sure you stay hydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What do I need to do when I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep using the swallowing techniques. Follow up with ENT in four weeks, and please see a gastroenterologist about the esophageal motility issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood sugar?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—talk to your primary doctor about that. Lifestyle changes may help, but you might need medication. We’ve included all this in your discharge instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep up the good work with your swallowing, and don’t hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The speech therapist will come by one more time to review the technique before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’d be helpful. I want to get this right."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. You’re doing great. We’re confident you’ll do well at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad I came in. I was really worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2169-10-18 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was the right call. We found some new things, and now we have a plan. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2169-10-15 18:42:00",
    "admission_end": "2169-10-18 16:46:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A young woman with a history of tracheobronchomalacia, bronchopulmonary dysplasia, and tracheostomy dependence was admitted for recurrent dysphagia and throat pain. She reported food sticking and odynophagia, with no recent oral intake. Initial evaluation showed no acute findings on labs or chest imaging. ENT evaluation revealed no structural cause, and a video swallow study showed no aspiration but frequent post-swallow coughing likely due to hypersensitivity. A barium swallow revealed moderate esophageal dysmotility, a new finding. She was advanced to a regular diet with improved symptoms using swallowing techniques involving trach occlusion. Pain was controlled with acetaminophen and ibuprofen. Hyperglycemia was noted with an A1c of 7.9, prompting outpatient follow-up. She was discharged home in stable condition with plans to see ENT, gastroenterology, and her primary care provider for diabetes evaluation.",
    "problems": [
      "Dyskinesia of esophagus",
      "Pain in throat",
      "Hyperglycemia, unspecified",
      "Unspecified asthma, uncomplicated",
      "Congenital tracheomalacia",
      "Congenital bronchomalacia",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Encounter for attention to tracheostomy",
      "Unspecified chronic bronchitis",
      "Bronchopulmonary dysplasia originating in the perinatal period",
      "Stenosis of larynx",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Overweight",
      "Body mass index [BMI] 34.0-34.9, adult"
    ]
  }
}
